Hello,

This is a modified version of Stefan's code to create a concordance of an unannotated text file. I think I've removed all the code that consisted of learning exercises etc. I also think this version retains punctuation .

I'd be interested in feedback as to whether there is still any unnecessary code . I believe the code removes punctuation. Is this correct?

Any assistance is appreciated.

Bob

# read in data
textfile <- scan("F:/Bolt/Bolt_noid.csv",what="character",skip=1,quiet=TRUE)

textfile.2<-gsub("(\\W)", "  \\1 ", textfile, perl=T) # a more complex way of getting at words
textfile.3<-unlist(strsplit(textfile.2, " +"))
tail(textfile.3)

# search
(matches.the<-grep("\\binstead\\b", textfile.3, ignore.case=T))

# output: simple

textfile.3[(matches.the[1]-10):(matches.the[2]+10)]

beginning.of.range<-max(1, (matches.the[1]-10)) # 1: the max rules out indices <= 0

# define an output file
output.file<-choose.files(default="C:/_qclwr/_outputfiles/04-2-1_output-e.txt") # for Windows users

for (i in matches.the) { # go through all matches in the file
   cat(file=output.file, append=T,
       textfile.3[max(0, i-10):max(0, i-1)], # note the max function with the 0!
       "\t",
       textfile.3[i],
       "\t",
       textfile.3[(i+1):min(length(textfile.3)+1, i+10)],
       "\n")
} # end of for: go through all matches

